add('manski','Share M1 M0 Monotone','Lower Upper','[Math.max(p[3]===1?0:-1,p[0]*p[1]-(1-p[0])*p[2]-p[0]),p[0]*p[1]+1-p[0]-(1-p[0])*p[2]]',lambda p:[max(0 if p[3]==1 else -1,p[0]*p[1]-(1-p[0])*p[2]-p[0]),p[0]*p[1]+1-p[0]-(1-p[0])*p[2]],'Binary toy outcomes have treated Share {Share}, treated mean M1 {M1}, control mean M0 {M0}. Monotone {Monotone}=1 assumes no harmful effects. What lower ATE bound results?','Unobserved counterfactual means range from zero to one. A no-harm assumption intersects these bounds with nonnegative effects; it must be justified.','p.slice(0,3).some(v=>v<0||v>1)||![0,1].includes(p[3])')
add('offpolicy','Target Behavior Reward','Weighted','[p[0]/p[1]*p[2]]',lambda p:[p[0]/p[1]*p[2]],'A toy action has Target probability {Target}, Behavior probability {Behavior}, observed Reward {Reward}. What importance-weighted reward results?','The probability ratio reweights a sample toward the target policy. Valid policy evaluation also requires support and correctly recorded behavior probabilities.','p[0]<0||p[0]>1||p[1]<=0||p[1]>1')
add('zstat','Estimate Null SE','Z','[(p[0]-p[1])/p[2]]',lambda p:[(p[0]-p[1])/p[2]],'A toy Estimate {Estimate} has standard error SE {SE}; the null value is {Null}. What standardized contrast results?','The same estimated contrast looks less precise with greater standard error. A test additionally needs a justified sampling distribution.','p[2]<=0')
add('meancontrast','SDA NA SDB NB','SE','[Math.sqrt(p[0]*p[0]/p[1]+p[2]*p[2]/p[3])]',lambda p:[math.sqrt(p[0]**2/p[1]+p[2]**2/p[3])],'Two independent toy means have SD/sample sizes {SDA}/{NA} and {SDB}/{NB}. What standard error of their difference results?','Independent sampling variances add for a difference. Reusing a control induces covariance among several treatment contrasts.','p.some(v=>v<=0)')
